# {{ display_name }}

An Apex competition generated by Concours. Solvers submit a `submission.py` that trains a model on the
public training data and scores new rows.

## Task

{{ task_description }}

## What you submit

A single Python file (`submission.py`, at most 5 MB) that defines `class Solver(SolverBase)` with
`fit(X, y)` and `predict_proba(X)`. Start from `player/submission.py`, the baseline. `SolverBase`
and the shared feature preparation live in `player/common/base.py`. Allowed libraries in the
player image: numpy, pandas, scikit-learn, LightGBM, XGBoost. No network access.

## How you are scored

- Primary metric: {{ metric_name }} ({{ metric_params }}). Higher is better.
{% if lift_package %}- How the lift is computed: every day, three review queues of {{ capacity }} cases are compared. Yours (ranked by
  score x amount), the "largest payments first" rule (a constant score) and the best possible queue (ranked by the
  true label). `raw_score = sum over days (yours - rule) / sum over days (best - rule)`. 0 means no better than
  reviewing the largest payments, 1 means every catchable payment was caught, negative means worse than the rule.
  A constant score lands at exactly 0. The fraud money per day of each queue is reported alongside.
{% endif %}- Secondary (shown for information): {{ secondary_name }}.
- Scoring happens inside the referee on rows you never see. Your submission is trained once on
  `player/data/train.csv` (the public training split, {{ train_rows }} rows, with the `label`
  column) at the start of evaluation and then asked to score batches of rows.
- The starting bar is today's model: {{ bar_text }}{% if bar_money_text %} ({{ bar_money_text }}){% endif %} on the hidden rows. A new leader must beat the bar, or the
  current top raw score if higher, by at least 1%.
- Leading here is not the same as becoming the customer's model. Concours promotes a version only after five gates
  on its own private holdout: hidden data, the same rows as the active model, a day-block luck test, no amount band
  or customer segment losing more than 5%, and scoring 10,000 rows in under 5 seconds.

## Data

- `player/data/train.csv`: {{ train_rows }} rows, columns `{{ feature_columns }}` plus `label`.
- `player/data/transform.json`: the columns Concours kept, dropped and masked, with reasons.
- Time column: {{ time_column }}. Hidden evaluation rows come after the training rows in time.

## Run the loop locally

```bash
docker build -f player/Dockerfile  -t {{ competition_id }}-player  .
docker build -f referee/Dockerfile -t {{ competition_id }}-referee .
docker network create --internal {{ competition_id }}-net
docker run -d --name player --network {{ competition_id }}-net --cpus {{ cpu_limit }} --memory {{ mem_limit }} \
  -v "$PWD/player/submission.py:/app/submission.py:ro" {{ competition_id }}-player
docker run --rm --network {{ competition_id }}-net \
  -e MATCH_ID=local -e SEED=0 -e NUM_PLAYERS=1 -e PLAYER_URLS='http://player:8000' \
  -e CONFIG_JSON="$(cat fixtures/input.json)" -v "$PWD/out:/data" {{ competition_id }}-referee
cat out/result.json
docker rm -f player && docker network rm {{ competition_id }}-net
```

Note: the referee image in a public copy of this repo must not contain `referee/data/holdout*`;
the competition owner transfers those separately.
